# Steering docs are deliberately kept out of this public repo -- they carry candid
# internal reasoning (VAC-risk research, safety-flag interruptions, killstreak/MP
# motivations) not meant for a public GitHub audience. Both files live one directory
# up from this repo root as of the 2026-08-05 move and are never meant to be copied
# back in, but ignored here too as a defensive safety net, same pattern as this
# file's other "never meant to land in the repo" entries below.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md

# Built release archives (d3d9.dll + friends, zipped per version) -- never meant to
# be committed. Confirmed 2026-09-15 they were being tracked in git and remained
# fully downloadable via the plain repo file browser at releases/ even after every
# -x86 release was archived on GitHub's own Releases tab and Nexus -- that browser
# view ignores Draft/Archived state entirely, so this was a real, live leak of
# builds this project has explicitly discontinued support for and refuses to serve.
# Full history purged the same day (git-filter-repo, path-scoped to releases/ only,
# every other file's content and every other commit's hash left untouched except
# for the necessary re-hashing that follows any file removed from history).
releases/

# Build outputs (proxy DLL is deployed straight into the game root, not committed)
proxy_d3d9/obj/
proxy_d3d9/Debug/
proxy_d3d9/Release/
*.obj
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.log
*.exp
*.lib
# Blanket rule, 2026-09-24: ALL .exe files are build output/binary artifacts and
# must never be committed, full stop -- direct instruction, following the real
# copyrighted-game-executable leak found the same day (re_notes/x64_migration/binaries/
# above). This replaces the prior per-tool-per-file listing below (a real,
# demonstrated failure mode: memdiff64.exe slipped through because only
# memdiff.exe was individually listed) -- kept as a blanket rule going forward,
# not more individual entries to maintain and miss.
*.exe
d3d9.dll
# Exception, 2026-09-23: the vendored, legitimately-committed DXVK build (real
# third-party library source, same as third_party/minhook/ -- not build output)
# happens to share the blanket d3d9.dll name the rule above targets. See
# proxy_d3d9.vcxproj's own DeployDxvk target for how this reaches the actual
# deployed game install directory (still never committed there).
!proxy_d3d9/third_party/dxvk/x64/d3d9.dll

# 2026-09-24: real, compiled, SIGNED NVIDIA Streamline/DLSS binaries
# (sl.interposer.dll, sl.common.dll, sl.dlss.dll, nvngx_dlss.dll, and their
# own .lib) -- deliberately vendored to disk for local development/testing
# but NEVER committed. Two real reasons, not just size (nvngx_dlss.dll alone
# is ~59MB): (1) these fall under NVIDIA's own DLSS SDK EULA, a separate,
# more restrictive license than the MIT-licensed SDK headers this repo does
# commit (proxy_d3d9/third_party/streamline/include/) -- including a real,
# still-unresolved "notify NVIDIA before commercial release" clause (see
# re_notes/x64_migration/vulkan_dlss_pipeline_research.md section 2.4); (2)
# this project's own hard-learned lesson from the 2026-09-24 leaked-game-
# binary incident above -- never commit a large, legally-sensitive binary to
# a public repo before its distribution terms are actually confirmed clear.
proxy_d3d9/third_party/streamline/bin/
proxy_d3d9/third_party/streamline/lib/

# Never commit a copy of any Microsoft system DLL, even accidentally staged for testing.
d3d9_orig.dll

# User-generated config (task #14) -- written fresh with defaults by mod_config.cpp
# on first run at the game root, never meant to be committed (personal tuning values).
mw3ncp_config.ini

# User's own scratch live-test notes (jotted during playtests, read back in during
# dev sessions) -- personal working notes, not a project doc, never meant to be committed.
notes.txt

# Build OUTPUTS ONLY for dev-only tools under tools/ -- these tools are not shipped
# with the mod itself, but their SOURCE is real, tracked, committed code (ui_harness
# in particular is a genuine standalone app with real ongoing development value, not
# a disposable script -- only its compiled .exe/.dll/.obj are excluded here, same
# "source tracked, build output ignored" policy this repo already applies to
# proxy_d3d9 itself). Double-star so this also covers nested sub-projects (e.g.
# tools/ui_harness/ui_hot/bin/), not just one level deep.
tools/**/bin/
tools/**/obj/

# memdiff full-process memory snapshots (~400MB each) -- diagnostic scratch data, never
# meant to be committed
tools/memdiff/*.snap

# xenia_probe (2026-08-03, Xenia/Xbox 360 console ground-truth research) -- its guest-RAM
# snapshots (~512MB each) and paired screenshots are diagnostic scratch data, same policy
# as memdiff's own .snap files above and the dumps/ policy below. Only the tool's own
# source (main.cpp) and throwaway analysis scripts are committed.
tools/xenia_probe/*.snap
tools/xenia_probe/*.bmp
tools/xenia_probe/*.png

# Third-party reference material (cloned locally for research only -- learn from and
# independently re-verify, never blindly reuse; see re_notes for how any lead from here
# gets treated). Not ours to redistribute as part of this repo.
references/

# Extracted MW3 game assets (from OpenAssetTools' Unlinker, run against our own retail
# .ff fastfiles for RE purposes -- see re_notes/iw5sp.md) are Activision's copyrighted
# game data, never ours to redistribute. Dumped outside this repo by default (D:\Tools),
# but ignored here too as a defensive safety net in case any dump output ever lands
# inside the repo by accident.
zone_dump/
ff_dump/
*.gdt

# Full-process MiniDumpWriteDump snapshots + matching screenshots (2026-08-02, issue #51
# live-memory-analysis toolchain) -- ~1-2GB each, kept locally on purpose for ongoing
# offline analysis (menu-position calibration, future killstreak/other investigation
# passes per project notes), never meant to be committed.
dumps/

# ui_harness diagram anchor editor output (2026-08-05, issue #66) -- a scratch
# hand-off file (drag positions in the harness, read the numbers back out here),
# never a source of truth on its own; the real defaults live in overlay_hud.cpp's
# own kDiagLayout* constexpr tables once copied over.
tools/ui_harness/exported_diagram_layout.txt

# Ghidra project for iw5sp.exe (2026-08-25, issue #90) -- a real, regenerable
# (~124s headless import+analysis) binary database, not source. Kept on disk
# across sessions so RE work doesn't re-pay the analysis time, but never
# committed -- too large (166MB+) and not meaningful to diff/review.
re_notes/ghidra_project/

# Same policy, x64 line (2026-09-03 recompile) -- iw5sp.exe AND iw5mp.exe Ghidra
# projects. FOUND UNPROTECTED 2026-09-12: this entry was missing entirely, and a
# .gbf database file inside it (80.95MB) had already been committed and pushed to
# the public repo, triggering GitHub's own "recommended maximum file size"
# warning -- fixed here going forward; the already-tracked file(s) still need a
# separate `git rm --cached` pass, not just this ignore rule (an ignore rule alone
# doesn't untrack something already committed).
re_notes/ghidra_project_x64/

# Same policy, real full (non-`-noanalysis`) analyzed Ghidra projects for both
# binaries (2026-09-24) -- kept on disk (each ~80MB) so future caller-search work
# doesn't re-pay the ~110s analysis time, added directly to this rule from the
# start this time rather than found unprotected after the fact like the entry
# above.
re_notes/x64_migration/ghidra_project_x86_analyzed/
re_notes/x64_migration/ghidra_project_x64_analyzed/

# CRITICAL, found 2026-09-24: the real, copyrighted Activision game executables
# (iw5sp.exe/iw5mp.exe, both the x64 and preserved-old-x86 copies) were tracked
# and committed to `main` back on 2026-09-03 (issue #111's own "preserved
# binaries" commit) and were live/downloadable from the public repo this whole
# time -- a real, active legal/copyright exposure, not caught until now. Ignored
# here immediately; the already-committed copies still need a full
# git-filter-repo history purge + force-push, same precedent as the 2026-09-15
# releases/ghidra_project_x64 incident -- see that entry's own reasoning, it
# applies here even more directly (these are literal unmodified game binaries,
# not documentation or a research database).
re_notes/x64_migration/binaries/

# Internal-only technical detail on unpatched vulnerabilities (exact function
# addresses, precise buffer/offset values, exact fix implementation logic) -- same
# redaction policy and file-naming convention as the sibling MW32011NSP project's
# own SECURITY.md/.gitignore (re_notes/INTERNAL_*.md, re_notes/internal/). Added
# proactively 2026-09-12, ahead of any NSP-into-NCP structural work, specifically
# so this protection is already in place before any of NSP's own internal files
# could ever land inside this repo's working tree -- never committed/pushed before
# a fix for that specific finding has shipped, regardless of which repo the file
# physically sits in.
re_notes/INTERNAL_*.md
re_notes/internal/
proxy_d3d9/src/git_version.h
.claude/worktrees/
